ing pollsters.\n\nExpert raters split between Likely R and Lean R, and prediction markets give Andrews roughly a 15 to 19 percent chance. The state's Republican lean and incumbency favor Graham, but the polling and money picture suggest a closer contest than past South Carolina Senate races, keeping this in Lean R territory with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1474, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2135, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2708, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2623, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2878, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2627, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2566, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.194, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2084, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1997, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2291, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2418, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.192, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.2237, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.2155, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.2123, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.2121, "margin": -4.0}]}